@startuml 04_activity_data_flow
' EKLT-VIO data flow, from one event message in the rosbag to a pose: every function (rounded box),
' the data it produces (square box), and the class that runs it (lane). Time flows downwards.
'
' Static code analysis, no run data. Code: jpl-x/x_events, branch events, commit fe2facf
' (inside the container: /catkin_ws/src/x), plus test/evaluate.cpp of this repo.
' Sources, in the order of the diagram:
'   test/evaluate.cpp:52, :317                       msgToEvents, processEventsMeasurement call
'   src/x/eklt/eklt_vio.cpp:164                      EKLTVIO::processEventsMeasurement
'   src/x/eklt/async_feature_tracker.cpp:91          AsyncFeatureTracker::processEvents
'   src/x/eklt/eklt_tracker.cpp:87                   EkltTracker::updatePatch
'   include/x/eklt/eklt_patch.h:65, :81, :114         contains, insert, getEventFrame
'   src/x/eklt/optimizer.cpp:71                      Optimizer::optimizeParameters (inside: see 08)
'   src/x/eklt/eklt_tracker.cpp:178                  setBatchSize
'   src/x/eklt/async_feature_interpolator.cpp:110    getMatchListFromPatches
'   src/x/ekf/ekf.cpp:153, :201                      processUpdateMeasurement, repropagateFromStateAtIdx
'   src/x/ekf/updater.cpp:21, :59                    Updater::update, applyUpdate
'   src/x/eklt/eklt_vio_updater.cpp:47, :80, :91, :270   preProcess, preUpdate, constructUpdate, postUpdate
'   src/x/vio/track_manager.cpp:90                   TrackManager::manageTracks
' Parameter names in the guards come from params_*.yaml (eklt_*), they are configuration, not data.
' View: VS Code PlantUML extension, Alt+D.
title EKLT-VIO data flow for one event message\nrounded box = function, square box = data it produces, lane = class running it

|evaluate.cpp|
start
#E3F0FB:dvs_msgs/EventArray read from the rosbag]
:msgToEvents()
evaluate.cpp:52;
#E3F0FB:x::EventArray
vector of Event: x, y, ts, polarity]
|EKLTVIO|
:processEventsMeasurement(events)
eklt_vio.cpp:164;
|AsyncFeatureTracker|
repeat :processEvents(): take the next Event e\nasync_feature_tracker.cpp:91;
  |EkltTracker / EkltPatch|
  :updatePatch(patch, e), for every active patch
  keeps e only if abs(e.x - cx) and abs(e.y - cy) are at most h = (P - 1) / 2
  and e.ts is not older than the patch
  eklt_tracker.cpp:87;
  #E3F0FB:EkltPatch::event_buffer_
  deque of Event, newest first, at most batch_size_]
  if (event_counter_ reached batch_size_ ?) then (yes)
    :getEventFrame(): each buffered event except the oldest adds
    +1 or -1 to the 4 pixels around it, with bilinear weights
    eklt_patch.h:114;
    #E3F0FB:event frame: P x P matrix of double
    timestamp t = mean of the newest and oldest buffered events]
    |Optimizer + Ceres|
    :optimizeParameters(frame, patch, t)
    Ceres solve of ErrorRotation, details in 08
    optimizer.cpp:71;
    note right
      also reads the reference log-gradient
      of the frame the patch was detected in
      (OptimizerDatum, built in 06)
    end note
    #E3F0FB:theta, tx, ty, phi, final_cost]
    |EkltTracker / EkltPatch|
    :warping_ = getWarp(theta, tx, ty), flow_angle_ = phi
    tracking_quality_ = 1 - final_cost / 2
    updateCenter(t): centre = inverse(warping_) * init_center_;
    #E3F0FB:AsyncPatch::track_hist_ gets (t, centre in pixels)]
    :setBatchSize(): next batch_size_ from the gradient and the flow
    discard the patch if quality is below eklt_tracking_quality
    or the centre left the image
    eklt_tracker.cpp:178;
  endif
  |AsyncFeatureTracker|
  if (eklt_ekf_update_every_n events since the last MatchList\nand at least one patch moved?) then (yes)
    |AsyncFeatureInterpolator|
    :getMatchListFromPatches()
    t* = newest patch time
    each patch: extrapolate track_hist_ linearly to t*, undistort
    previous = the Feature this patch got last time
    async_feature_interpolator.cpp:110;
    #E3F0FB:x::MatchList, kept until the end of the message
    one Match(previous, current) per patch
    Features in undistorted pixels]
  endif
  |AsyncFeatureTracker|
repeat while (events left in the message?) is (yes)
->no;
#E3F0FB:vector of MatchList, returned to EKLTVIO]
|EKLTVIO|
repeat :take the next MatchList;
  :wrap it with t* + time_offset and the current frame;
  #E3F0FB:x::VioMeasurement]
  |Ekf|
  :processUpdateMeasurement(): closestIdx(t*) in the StateBuffer
  ekf.cpp:153;
  #E3F0FB:copy of the buffered x::State closest to t*
  prior from IMU propagation, see 06]
  |EkltVioUpdater|
  :update() -> preProcess()
  eklt_vio_updater.cpp:47;
  |TrackManager / StateManager|
  :TrackManager::manageTracks()
  attach each Match to the track whose last Feature equals match.previous,
  grow or start opportunistic tracks, promote long ones to SLAM or MSCKF,
  then Camera::normalize()
  track_manager.cpp:90;
  #E3F0FB:TrackLists in normalised image coordinates
  SLAM tracks, MSCKF tracks, new SLAM tracks (MSCKF-initialised or depth prior)
  + indexes of lost SLAM tracks]
  :preUpdate() -> StateManager::manage()
  slide the pose window, remove lost SLAM features
  from the state and the covariance
  eklt_vio_updater.cpp:80;
  |EkltVioUpdater|
  :constructUpdate(): stack the MsckfUpdate, MsckfSlamUpdate
  and SlamUpdate rows, then applyQRDecomposition()
  eklt_vio_updater.cpp:91;
  #E3F0FB:H (rows x n_err), res (rows x 1), R (rows x rows)]
  :Updater::applyUpdate()
  S = H P H^T + R, K = P H^T S^-1
  correction = K res, P = (I - K H) P, State::correct()
  updater.cpp:59;
  #E3F0FB:corrected x::State]
  :postUpdate(): insert the new SLAM features
  into the state and the covariance
  eklt_vio_updater.cpp:270;
  |Ekf|
  :repropagateFromStateAtIdx(): write the state back,
  re-propagate every newer buffered state with its IMU sample
  ekf.cpp:201;
  #E3F0FB:newest x::State]
  |EKLTVIO|
repeat while (MatchLists left?) is (yes)
->no;
|evaluate.cpp|
:addPose(): one row of pose.csv;
stop
@enduml
